/******************************************************************************
* djinterp [re_std]                                                     climits
*
* <climits> umbrella header:
*   Aggregates the granular headers under /inc/djinterp/re_std/climits/.
* Mirrors the standard <climits> convenience header and adds no symbols of
* its own.
*
*   A MACRO-ONLY MODULE HAS NO NAMESPACED SURFACE:
*   Every name <climits> provides is a preprocessor macro, so this module
* contributes no re_std:: symbols at all -- unlike <cstddef>, which has a
* typedef half. What it contributes instead is a guarantee: after
* including this header, the C++11 macro set is present even on a library
* that predates it (see climits.hpp), and it is present with the
* platform's own values wherever the platform supplied them.
*
*   The full set surfaced here:
*
*     CHAR_BIT, MB_LEN_MAX
*     CHAR_MIN / CHAR_MAX          (signedness of plain char is
*                                   implementation-defined; do not assume)
*     SCHAR_MIN / SCHAR_MAX / UCHAR_MAX
*     SHRT_MIN  / SHRT_MAX  / USHRT_MAX
*     INT_MIN   / INT_MAX   / UINT_MAX
*     LONG_MIN  / LONG_MAX  / ULONG_MAX
*     LLONG_MIN / LLONG_MAX / ULLONG_MAX          (C++11)
*
*   For anything that is not a preprocessor conditional, reach for
* re_std::numeric_limits<T> from <limits> instead: it is typed,
* namespaced, constexpr, and it works uniformly for the floating-point
* types, which have no macro equivalent here at all.
*
*
* path:      /inc/djinterp/re_std/climits/climits
* link(s):   TBA
* author(s): TBA                                           created: 2026.08.25
******************************************************************************/

